{"id": "DfW5pr3xRAe", "title": "Video by therishikatha", "description": "Why does Ganesha have only ONE tusk? Because Parshurama threw Shiva's own axe at him… and Ganesha let it strike 🐘🪓 Part 7 of the Parshurama series.\n\nAfter his wars, Parshurama climbed Mount Kailash to see his guru, Shiva. At the palace door stood Ganesha: \"Wait! My parents are resting.\" \"I'll just bow to them and come right back.\" \"No.\" He pushed in, Ganesha pushed back, and Kartikeya had to pull them apart.\n\nParshurama raised his axe. Ganesha picked him up, carried him through every world, up to the heavens and down below, dropped him in the waters, and set him back exactly where he had stood. Soaked and dizzy, Parshurama threw his axe.\n\nGanesha knew that axe. His father, Shiva, had given it to Parshurama. He would not let his father's gift go in vain, so he took it on his tusk. The tusk fell and the earth shook. Parvati was furious: \"Your own disciple broke our son's tusk with the axe you gave him!\" Shiva said nothing. He called Krishna, who came with Radha and said: \"Today your son has become EKADANTA, the one-tusked.\" Radha healed Ganesha's cheek with a touch, and Parvati forgave Parshurama and blessed him.\n\n📖 Source: Brahmanda Purana, Upodghata Pada, chapters 41–42 (the Brahma Vaivarta Purana tells it too).\n\n📚 Stories of Shakti for little ones: the Navadurga Set from Rishi Katha is out now. Check the link in bio (rishikatha.com).\n\n💬 Ekadanta is one of his names. How many other names of Ganesha do you know? Comment them 👇\n🔁 Save it for Part 8 and share it with someone who loves Bappa.\n\n#ganesha #ganpatibappamorya #ekadanta #parshuram #parshurama #lordshiva #mahadev #ganeshji #vinayaka #hindumythology #sanatandharma #indianmythology #mythologystories #rishikatha #hinduism", "channel": "therishikatha", "uploader_id": "22569163881", "uploader": "Rishi Katha", "timestamp": 1793877444, "like_count": 7265, "comment_count": 28, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.inst